@@ -66,9 +66,12 @@ ## Discord ops alerts
 
 | Item | Detail |
 | --- | --- |
-| Env | `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` → `config('services.discord.webhook_url')` |
+| Env | `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` maps to `config('services.discord.webhook_url')`, `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` maps to `config('services.discord.mention_id')` |
 | Client | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send($title, $message, $context = [])` |
+| Mention | `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` -> `config('services.discord.mention_id')` — optional Discord user ID pinged as `<@ID>` on its own line after the rest of the content |
 | Unconfigured | Empty/missing URL → silent no-op (safe for CI) |
+| Mention validation | Only a 17-20 digit snowflake (whitespace trimmed; integer accepted) emits a mention - anything else (@everyone, @here, short numbers, embedded newlines/extra chars) is ignored silently |
+| Truncation | Content capped at 1800 chars total; with a mention, room is reserved so the mention survives and the title/message/context part is truncated instead |
 | Failures | Non-2xx / transport errors are logged without the webhook URL; they do not throw |
 
 Call from jobs/handlers when a notable ops event occurs; do not wire every exception globally.
